  "sharedGrammar": "Object-literal returns over: number/string/boolean/null literals, parameter identifiers, non-computed member access, binary + - * /, comparisons, && ||, unary ! -, plus the v2 whitelisted deterministic numeric builtin table (sqrt, sin, cos, acos, abs, floor, min, max over finite f64, fail-closed on non-finite or negative-zero results; subset id holoscript-engine-hsplus-deterministic-action-subset-v2-numeric-builtins in both lanes). No other calls, no loops, no host bindings. The two executable projections have measured, non-identical grammars: the engine deterministic action subset accepts ternary expressions but restricts assignment to declared state, while the compiler-wasm trait evaluator accepts local assignment and if/else statements but has no ternary or ===/!== production. Ops whose default body uses ternary or locals therefore carry an equivalent traitBody statement form; cross-target conformance is claimed on produced values over the shared vector corpus, not on shared surface syntax. Builtin results that depend on libm transcendentals (sin/cos/acos) may differ by ulps between the JS engine and the Rust-libm-in-wasm lane, so those vectors carry an explicit non-zero tolerance; sqrt is IEEE-754 correctly rounded and stays exact.",
  "numericBuiltins": true,
  "localBindings": true,
  "vectorPolicy": "Every vector must produce finite, non-negative-zero values under IEEE-754 double semantics with strict source-order evaluation. Expected values are computed from the TypeScript reference twin at generation time and verified bit-exact against the engine deterministic runtime before admission; tolerance 0 means exact equality including key sets.",
